# musl (cimo/runtime)
#
# cimo's runtime library (this directory) is compiled by cimo itself and linked into every
# compiled module. Most of it comes from musl 1.2.5 (https://musl.libc.org/, release tarball
# sha256 a9a118bbe84d8764da0ea0d28b3ab3fae8477fc7e4085d90102b8596fc7c75e4):
#
# - math/: musl src/math (generic C), unchanged, except the functions cimo compiles to single
#   instructions (sqrt, fabs, fmin, fmax, floor, ceil, trunc, round, fma and their float
#   versions) and nearbyint, which are small cimo files.
# - string/: musl src/string, with the word-at-a-time paths enabled for cimo (they are
#   guarded by __GNUC__ in musl); strcoll, strxfrm and strerror are cimo's ("C" locale, no errno).
# - ctype/ctype.c: musl src/ctype, merged into one file.
# - stdlib/: musl src/stdlib and src/internal/{intscan,floatscan}.c over a string-only
#   pseudo-FILE; long double replaced by double in floatscan.c, whose hex-float digit window
#   is one digit wider (musl's is too narrow for a binary64 long double: "0x1.00000000000008001p0"
#   rounded down).
# - stdio/vfprintf.c: musl src/stdio/vfprintf.c, writing to a sink instead of a FILE.
# - internal/: cut-down versions of musl's internal headers.
